            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I'm running into the same issue. Has this regressed? Happy to help debug in any way I can.\n\nNo, it should have not. Mostly because nothing seems to touch that part of the code and I can not reproduce. Opening 'tsx' file loads tree-sitter parser as expected.\n\nIf you are sure that you have updated to the latest 'mini.nvim' `main` and have properly installed tree-sitter parser, then providing a minimal reproduction will be useful.\n\nBut before that, I'd highly recommend trying it with [MiniMax](https://nvim-mini.org/MiniMax/):\n- [Set it up](https://nvim-mini.org/MiniMax/#setting-up) in separate config directory (`nvim-minimax`).\n- Apply the following diff:\n\n    ```diff\n    diff --git a/plugin/40_plugins.lua b/plugin/40_plugins.lua\n    index b6dfe8a..6bcf8ba 100644\n    --- a/plugin/40_plugins.lua\n    +++ b/plugin/40_plugins.lua\n    @@ -49,6 +49,7 @@ now_if_args(function()\n         'lua',\n         'vimdoc',\n         'markdown',\n    +    'tsx',\n         -- Add here more languages with which you want to use tree-sitter\n         -- To see available languages:\n         -- - Execute `:=require('nvim-treesitter').get_available()`\n    ```\n\n- Restart. It should install 'tsx' parser.\n- Open any '*.tsx' file and try to selection function definition with `vaF`. It works for me.",
